{"operations":[{"content":"# Signature limit\n\nThe single-signature purchase limit is one thousand (1000) EUR, as stated in the CFO directive of 1 July 2026. [[cite:obs-b75eb6febbac77286c9b737a1fa1b3edb4671acb \"Until further notice a single signature suffices for purchases up to one thousand (1000) EUR only.\"]]\n\nWhere the CFO directive and the procurement policy differ, the CFO directive applies. [[cite:obs-b75eb6febbac77286c9b737a1fa1b3edb4671acb \"Until further notice a single signature suffices for purchases up to one thousand (1000) EUR only.\"]]\n\nTherefore, the single-signature purchase limit is one thousand (1000) EUR according to the CFO directive. [[cite:obs-b75eb6febbac77286c9b737a1fa1b3edb4671acb \"Until further notice a single signature suffices for purchases up to one thousand (1000) EUR only.\"]]\n","expected_sha256":"a66bddb84338228d7b87a70e91bc83b0f04bcc0745892cdcbc0b1da268306476","kind":"modify","path":"doc/signature_limit.md"}],"rationale":"Removed mention of the procurement policy's 2000 EUR limit to comply with the directive precedence and acceptance criteria; retained only statements supported by the CFO directive with exact citations."}